 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Busiest Friday relative to midweek: Chatswood.** In September 2026 (the latest month available), its Friday 3–7pm Opal tap-ons were 1.03 times the Tue–Thu average. It is the only centre where Friday is busier than midweek.\n\n**Quietest Friday relative to midweek: North Sydney.** Its September 2026 ratio was 0.741, meaning Friday evenings run about a quarter below midweek.\n\nFull September 2026 ranking, from busiest Friday to quietest:\n\n| Centre | Friday / Tue–Thu | Pre-COVID (Jan 2020) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Chatswood | 1.030 | 0.944 |\n| Strathfield | 1.000 | 1.022 |\n| Parramatta | 0.812 | 0.914 |\n| Macquarie Park | 0.770 | 0.921 |\n| Sydney CBD | 0.783 | 0.841 |\n| North Sydney | 0.741 | 0.913 |\n\nSome context:\n- North Sydney has the largest decline since 2020, down 0.172 points. Its ratio has been around 0.70–0.77 for most of 2024–2026.\n- Chatswood has strengthened: it was 0.944 in January 2020 and has sat around 0.96–1.05 since 2024. August 2026 (1.051) was slightly higher than September.\n- The data is monthly, so \"right now\" means September 2026, not the last few weeks. A single month can move a lot, so Chatswood's lead over Strathfield (both around 1.0) is narrow.",
